---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '../components/Breadcrumb.astro';
import { SITE_URL, SITE_NAME, CONTACT, ORGANIZATION } from '../site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How WorldFreightHub collects, uses, shares and retains the information you submit through the quote form — and your GDPR and CCPA rights over that information."
  canonical={`${SITE_URL}/privacy-policy/`}
>
  <div class="page-header">
    <div class="container">
      <Breadcrumb items={[{ label: 'Privacy Policy' }]} />
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        WorldFreightHub is a freight information reference. This page explains,
        in plain terms, exactly what personal information we collect, what we
        do with it, what we deliberately do not collect, how long we keep it,
        and the rights you have over it under the GDPR and the CCPA.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="section container">
    <h2>1. Who operates this site</h2>
    <p>
      {SITE_NAME} ({SITE_URL}) is operated by{' '}
      <strong>{ORGANIZATION.legalName}</strong>, a trading company established
      in {ORGANIZATION.foundingDate} and located at{' '}
      {ORGANIZATION.address.streetAddress}, {ORGANIZATION.address.addressLocality},{' '}
      {ORGANIZATION.address.addressRegion}, China. The company acts as the
      data controller for any personal information submitted through this site.
    </p>
    <p>
      For any privacy question or data request, contact us at{' '}
      <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT.email}`}>{CONTACT.email}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Scope of this policy</h2>
    <p>
      This policy covers the personal information we collect through this
      website, including the{' '}
      <a href="/get-quote/">get-quote form</a>. It does not cover the privacy
      practices of third-party websites we link to — port authorities, customs
      authorities, carriers and directory providers — which have their own
      privacy policies. It also does not cover any information you provide
      directly to a freight provider after we route your quote request to them.
    </p>

    <h2>3. What personal information we collect</h2>
    <p>
      We collect only the information you voluntarily submit through the quote
      form, plus the standard technical logs every web server records. We do
      not require an account and we do not collect payment details of any
      kind.
    </p>

    <h3>3.1 Information you submit through the quote form</h3>
    <p>
      When you request a freight quote, the form asks for the following fields:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Name</strong> (required) — so the provider can address you.</li>
      <li><strong>Email</strong> (required) — so the provider can reply to you.</li>
      <li><strong>WhatsApp or phone number</strong> (optional) — an alternative
      contact channel, if you choose to provide one.</li>
      <li><strong>Origin and destination</strong> (required) — the ports or
      cities of your shipment.</li>
      <li><strong>Cargo description</strong> (required) — what you are shipping.</li>
      <li><strong>Weight and volume</strong> (required) — the shipment size.</li>
      <li><strong>Incoterm and method</strong> (required) — the delivery terms
      and mode of transport.</li>
      <li><strong>Additional notes</strong> (optional) — any extra detail you
      choose to add, such as cargo value or a target delivery date.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      You submit this information by your own action, and it is used for the
      single purpose described in section 5. The more precise the weight,
      volume and cargo detail, the more accurate the provider's quote can be —
      but you are never required to provide more than the form marks as
      required.
    </p>

    <h3>3.2 Server logs</h3>
    <p>
      Like almost every website, our hosting infrastructure records standard
      technical logs for each request. These logs typically include your IP
      address, the page requested, the time of the request, the browser and
      operating system you use, and a referring URL. These logs are used only
      for security, debugging and keeping the site available. They are not
      linked to your identity and are not used to build a profile of you.
    </p>

    <h2>4. How the quote form works (and who it passes through)</h2>
    <p>
      The quote form is processed by a third-party form service,{' '}
      <strong>FormSubmit</strong> (formsubmit.co). When you press submit, your
      submission is transmitted to FormSubmit, which forwards it to our contact
      inbox at <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT.email}`}>{CONTACT.email}</a>.
      FormSubmit therefore processes your form data as a data processor on our
      behalf. Its servers may be located outside your country of residence, so
      submitting the form involves an international transfer of your details —
      see section 8.
    </p>
    <p>
      After we receive your request, we share the relevant shipment details
      with <strong>one freight provider on the corridor you selected</strong> so
      that the provider can quote you. This is the sole purpose of the form.
      We do not share your details with multiple providers for the same
      request, and we do not sell, rent or publish your contact details.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Purposes and legal basis for processing</h2>
    <p>
      We process your personal information for the following purposes, each
      with a clear legal basis:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Responding to your quote request</strong> — performed with
      your consent (you submitted the form) and to take steps toward the
      service you requested (a freight quote).</li>
      <li><strong>Routing the request to a provider</strong> — performed because
      you asked us to connect you with a provider; this is the core of the
      service the form offers.</li>
      <li><strong>Security and site availability</strong> — server logs are
      processed on the basis of our legitimate interest in keeping the site
      secure and operational, and in preventing abuse of the quote form.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>6. What we do NOT collect or do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>No analytics or advertising trackers.</strong> This site runs
      no analytics scripts and no advertising or marketing trackers.</li>
      <li><strong>No advertising cookies.</strong> We do not set advertising
      cookies, and we do not sell personal data — including under the CCPA's
      definition of "sale".</li>
      <li><strong>No behavioural profiles.</strong> We do not build profiles of
      visitors, and we do not engage in automated decision-making about you.</li>
      <li><strong>No payment information.</strong> We never collect or process
      payment card or bank details.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>7. How long we keep information</h2>
    <p>
      Quote requests are kept only as long as needed to route them to a
      provider and respond — typically a few weeks. If a request does not
      result in an ongoing engagement, the form data is not retained
      indefinitely and can be deleted on request. Server logs are retained for
      a short, fixed period for security purposes and then rotated out.
    </p>
    <p>
      You can ask us to delete your request at any time by emailing{' '}
      <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT.email}`}>{CONTACT.email}</a>, and we will
      remove it from our inbox and ask any provider we routed it to to do the
      same where that is within our control.
    </p>

    <h2>8. International transfers</h2>
    <p>
      Our operator is based in China, and the freight corridor we cover runs
      from China to the Gulf Cooperation Council states. Your form submission
      may therefore be processed in, or transferred to, the following
      locations:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>China</strong> — where the operator receives and reviews your
      request.</li>
      <li><strong>The provider's location</strong> — a freight provider on your
      selected corridor, which may be in China, the GCC or elsewhere, receives
      the shipment details needed to quote you.</li>
      <li><strong>FormSubmit's servers</strong> — which may be outside your
      country of residence, as a result of using their form-processing
      service.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Where your information is transferred across borders, we transfer only
      the minimum needed for the purpose, and we rely on the service or the
      routing you requested as the basis for that transfer.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Your rights under the GDPR</h2>
    <p>
      If you are located in the European Economic Area or the United Kingdom,
      you have the following rights over your personal information:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Access</strong> — request a copy of the personal information
      we hold about you.</li>
      <li><strong>Rectification</strong> — ask us to correct inaccurate or
      incomplete information.</li>
      <li><strong>Erasure</strong> — ask us to delete your information where
      there is no overriding reason to keep it.</li>
      <li><strong>Restriction</strong> — ask us to limit how we process your
      information in certain circumstances.</li>
      <li><strong>Portability</strong> — receive your submitted information in
      a structured, commonly used format.</li>
      <li><strong>Objection</strong> — object to processing based on legitimate
      interests.</li>
      <li><strong>Withdraw consent</strong> — withdraw your consent to the
      processing of your form submission at any time.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      To exercise any of these rights, email{' '}
      <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT.email}`}>{CONTACT.email}</a>. We respond to
      such requests within a reasonable time, and we will verify your identity
      before acting on a request about your data.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Your rights under the CCPA / CPRA</h2>
    <p>
      If you are a California resident, you have the right to:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Know</strong> — request disclosure of the categories and
      specific pieces of personal information we have collected about you.</li>
      <li><strong>Delete</strong> — request deletion of the personal information
      we collected from you.</li>
      <li><strong>Opt out of "sale" and "sharing"</strong> — we do not sell or
      share your personal information for cross-context behavioural advertising,
      so there is nothing to opt out of; this is stated plainly here.</li>
      <li><strong>Non-discrimination</strong> — we will not discriminate against
      you for exercising any of these rights.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We do not "sell" or "share" personal information as those terms are
      defined under the CCPA. To exercise a CCPA right, email{' '}
      <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT.email}`}>{CONTACT.email}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Children's privacy</h2>
    <p>
      This site is a business-to-business freight reference and is not
      directed at children. We do not knowingly collect personal information
      from children under the age of 16. If you believe a child has submitted
      personal information to us, contact us and we will delete it.
    </p>

    <h2>12. Security measures</h2>
    <p>
      We take reasonable technical and organisational measures to protect the
      information you submit, including:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Minimisation.</strong> We collect only the fields needed to
      produce a quote, and nothing more.</li>
      <li><strong>No payment data.</strong> We never collect or store payment
      information, which removes the most sensitive category of data entirely.</li>
      <li><strong>Restricted access.</strong> Quote submissions are received in
      a single contact inbox and are not published or exposed.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      No method of transmission over the internet is completely secure, but we
      apply these measures to keep the risk proportionate to the minimal data
      we hold.
    </p>

    <h2>13. Third-party links and services</h2>
    <p>
      Pages on this site link to external sources such as port authorities,
      customs authorities and carriers. Their privacy practices are their own,
      and this policy does not cover them. The two third-party services that
      process data in connection with this site are described in our{' '}
      <a href="/cookie-policy/">cookie policy</a>: FormSubmit (form processing)
      and Google Fonts (fonts on Arabic-language pages).
    </p>

    <h2>14. Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      If we change how we handle personal information, this page is updated
      with a new revision date. Material changes are announced on the{' '}
      <a href="/data-changelog/">data changelog</a>. We do not apply changes
      retroactively to information collected under an earlier version of this
      policy without a lawful basis to do so.
    </p>

    <h2>15. Contact for privacy</h2>
    <p>
      Privacy questions and data requests:{' '}
      <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT.email}`}>{CONTACT.email}</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Related policies:{' '}
      <a href="/terms-of-use/">Terms of Use</a> ·{' '}
      <a href="/cookie-policy/">Cookie Policy</a> ·{' '}
      <a href="/disclaimer/">Disclaimer</a> ·{' '}
      <a href="/corrections/">Corrections</a>.
    </p>
    <p class="muted">Last updated: 23 October 2026</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
